cff-version: 1.2.0
title: postcode-privacy
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both it and the method it
  implements. The graph-metric approach is Takagi et al.'s, not ours.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Stenson
    given-names: Iain
repository-code: "https://github.com/Iain-S/postcode-privacy"
url: "https://iain-s.github.io/postcode-privacy/"
abstract: >-
  Local differential privacy for UK postcodes, measuring privacy in hops
  along a graph of postcode units rather than in metres. An implementation
  of Geo-Graph-Indistinguishability over ONS Postcode Directory geography,
  with a population-weighted prior, an exactly-computable capped metric and
  keyed-deterministic perturbation.
keywords:
  - differential privacy
  - geoprivacy
  - postcodes
  - anonymisation
license: MIT
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Geo-Graph-Indistinguishability: Location Privacy on Road Networks
      Based on Differential Privacy
    authors:
      - family-names: Takagi
        given-names: Shun
      - family-names: Cao
        given-names: Yang
      - family-names: Asano
        given-names: Yasuhito
      - family-names: Yoshikawa
        given-names: Masatoshi
    year: 2020
    identifiers:
      - type: other
        value: "arXiv:2010.13449"
  - type: conference-paper
    title: Broadening the Scope of Differential Privacy Using Metrics
    authors:
      - family-names: Chatzikokolakis
        given-names: Konstantinos
      - family-names: Andrés
        given-names: Miguel E.
      - family-names: Bordenabe
        given-names: Nicolás Emilio
      - family-names: Palamidessi
        given-names: Catuscia
    collection-title: Privacy Enhancing Technologies Symposium (PETS)
    year: 2013
